From f9d5f492f43805c3bd570f128a855fa7d44f0d3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:54:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] system log: Find and Exclude take comma lists; saved
 exclusions, the user's own logFilter.json

Find shows a line holding any of its comma-separated words and Exclude hides
a line holding any of its words (case ignored; Exclude wins). Saved
exclusions are one pattern per line in /jffs/reaper/logfilter, read and
written by the new reaper_logf.cgi behind the http_id gate (64 entries of up
to 128 printable ASCII characters, checked again on save; an empty list
removes the file). Stock's logFilter.json sits in the read-only image, so no
user could add to it. Only the view changes: the log file, Save and a remote
syslog server still get every line. The list rides the Reaper settings file
(section log, key rlog_filter, validated on import).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
